From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John Rowley <johnrowleyster@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 12:50:22 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(miniwin): draw immediate mode on Citro3D

SubmitImmediate, SetViewportRect and ClearRect on the Citro3D backend,
and the backend listed in Miniwin_DeviceDrawsImmediateMode:

- The vertices are lit and culled on the CPU (ImmediateTransformer), as
  on the other backends, projected and turned onto the sideways
  framebuffer, and drawn from a per-frame linear buffer through a
  pass-through shader. Depth is reversed, as citro3d's own projections
  give retained mode, so both share the z-buffer.
- Texture stage 0 becomes PICA texture combiners; a colour key, an alpha
  test; fog, a table indexed by depth. The arithmetic is in
  citro3dimmediate.h, which builds on any host.
- Viewports are a viewport and scissor on the framebuffer, for retained
  draws too; a rectangle clear is a quad among the draws.
- A level's frame outgrows citro3d's default command buffer: it is 1 MiB,
  and a draw that would overflow it is dropped with a warning instead of
  stopping the program.
- 2D images are uploaded at their own size and sampled half a texel in
  from the source rectangle, on whole pixels, so that a font drawn at
  half size never shows its glyph separators.
- The backend no longer shadows the base renderer's viewport transform,
  so GetFitRect sees the fit.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

